{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":248446,"duration_api_ms":248379,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls, `pkg/format/` provides shared formatting, `pkg/testutils/` is the differential testing harness, `magefiles/` drives builds.\n\n**Current State**: All packages in releases 00.0–01.3 have source code present: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/version`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`. All have both implementation and differential tests.\n\n**Gap Identified**: The architecture specifies `pkg/sys/` should provide \"Signal handling (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH)\" but this capability is absent from `pkg/sys/`. Instead, SIGPIPE handlers are duplicated in `cmd/cat/main.go` (line 166–173), `cmd/du/main.go` (line 215–222), and `cmd/sponge/main.go` (line 338–346) — violating DD3 (shared pkg/ for common logic) and SC4 (no duplication of syscall code across cmd/). Furthermore, `cmd/wc/main.go` is **missing** SIGPIPE handling entirely — the package comment claims `prd005-wc R5` but the test file (`wc_test.go` line 6) omits R5, and no signal-related code exists in the implementation.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd002-sys, prd005-wc R5: Consolidate SIGPIPE handling into pkg/sys and add to cmd/wc\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (signal handling requirements for pkg/sys)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd005-wc.yaml (R5 -- signal/operational requirements missing from cmd/wc)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys capabilities list includes \"Signal handling (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH)\" and DD3 requiring shared pkg/ for common logic)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (existing pkg/sys exported function pattern)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (existing pkg/sys exported function and platform abstraction pattern)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (lines 166-173: installSIGPIPEHandler to consolidate)\n      - cmd/du/main.go (lines 215-222: installSIGPIPEHandler to consolidate)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (missing SIGPIPE handling -- prd005-wc R5 not implemented)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/signal.go\n        action: create\n        note: Shared SIGPIPE signal handler function exported for use by cmd/ packages\n      - path: pkg/sys/signal_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for SIGPIPE signal handler registration\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys (implements prd005-wc R5)\n      - path: cmd/cat/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Replace local installSIGPIPEHandler with call to pkg/sys shared function\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Replace local installSIGPIPEHandler with call to pkg/sys shared function\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create pkg/sys/signal.go exporting a function that registers a SIGPIPE signal handler. The handler calls os.Exit(0) when SIGPIPE is received. Follow the existing pattern from cmd/cat/main.go lines 166-173: make(chan os.Signal, 1), signal.Notify for syscall.SIGPIPE, goroutine that blocks on channel receive then exits 0.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Replace the local installSIGPIPEHandler function in cmd/cat/main.go (lines 166-173) and cmd/du/main.go (lines 215-222) with a call to the new pkg/sys function. Remove the local function definition and any imports that become unused (os/signal, syscall) after the switch. Add the pkg/sys import.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add a call to the new pkg/sys SIGPIPE handler function at the start of the run() function in cmd/wc/main.go, before flag parsing. cmd/wc currently has no SIGPIPE handling; this implements prd005-wc R5. Add the pkg/sys import.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Create pkg/sys/signal_test.go with tests verifying that the SIGPIPE handler function can be called without panic and that repeated calls do not panic. Follow the existing test patterns from pkg/sys/terminal_test.go and pkg/sys/fileinfo_test.go.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/signal.go uses no build tags (_darwin.go/_linux.go) because syscall.SIGPIPE and the os/signal package are portable across Darwin and Linux. This differs from fileinfo.go which requires build-tagged variants for Stat_t field divergence.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"The SIGPIPE handler exits with code 0, matching the behavior specified in prd006-cat R5.4 and prd009-du R5.1. This is the standard Unix convention: SIGPIPE causes silent exit, not an error.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The call to the SIGPIPE handler must be the first statement in each cmd/ run() function, before flag parsing and any I/O. This matches the existing placement in cmd/cat/main.go line 54 and cmd/du/main.go line 48, ensuring the handler is active before any write operation that could trigger SIGPIPE.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/signal.go exists and exports a SIGPIPE handler installation function\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"pkg/sys/signal_test.go exists and all tests pass with go test ./pkg/sys/\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"cmd/cat/main.go no longer contains a local installSIGPIPEHandler function; it calls the pkg/sys function instead\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"cmd/du/main.go no longer contains a local installSIGPIPEHandler function; it calls the pkg/sys function instead\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"cmd/wc/main.go calls the pkg/sys SIGPIPE handler at the start of run()\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/cat/ ./cmd/du/ ./cmd/wc/ ./pkg/sys/ all succeed with no errors\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/sys/ ./cmd/cat/ ./cmd/du/ ./cmd/wc/ all pass\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"888376c3-396f-455b-b9a0-8c1cc11c4d56","total_cost_usd":0.97704975,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85439,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"output_tokens":17336,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85439,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":17336,"cacheReadInputTokens":19292,"cacheCreationInputTokens":85439,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.97704975,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"b26834b9-8ee9-4270-b971-8e6f8ee3914f"}
